@node CMacs Calculator
@chapter CMacs Calculator: Desktop, Financial, Physics & CAS

@cindex calculator
@cindex calc
@cindex financial
@cindex physics
@cindex relativity
@cindex tax
@cindex computer algebra

@code{cmacs-calculator} is a @emph{calculator you can actually use}: a desktop
calculator with correct precedence, 121 named calculators across finance,
physics, relativity and tax, every GNU Calc built-in function
(@pxref{Calculator Builtins}), a full computer-algebra system, unit conversion
with CODATA constants (@pxref{Calculator Constants}), and charts.  It is reachable from a sheet buffer, from
any major mode inline, from a terminal REPL (@code{emacs --calc}), and from an
AI agent over MCP.

The engine is @strong{GNU Calc} (@file{lisp/calc/}), which Emacs already ships:
an arbitrary-precision CAS with symbolic algebra, a units table with CODATA
physical constants, matrices and complex numbers.  cmacs wraps it
@emph{additively} and never modifies @file{lisp/calc/} --- cmacs tracks upstream
Emacs, so upstream files stay untouched.

It is a @emph{mostly-Elisp subsystem}; its small C half provides the
@code{emacs --calc} entry point, the libregnum GPU chart bridge, and the MCP
tools.  Enable it with @option{--with-cmacs-calculator}; the flag is exposed as
@code{IS-CMACS-CALCULATOR} and @code{(cmacs-feature-p 'calculator)}.  libregnum
is @emph{optional} --- the SVG chart tier stands alone.

